# Fizzleworth-attack-ultima.lic
# Bigshot custom attack routine for Fizzleworth (Sorcerer). A FOURTH variant
# for the gs4-wings-compare experiment -- Fizzleworth-attack-base with a
# creature-specific disable step and a one-shot animate buddy bolted on.
# Drop it into a bigshot hunting-commands list as a single command:
#
#   script Fizzleworth-attack-ultima
#
# Plugging it into a profile is the only setup needed.
#
# --- what's different from -base -----------------------------------------
#
# -base opens every target with Web (118) regardless of what it is. -ultima
# instead picks the disable by creature, then runs the SAME 710 -> 706 -> hold
# DoT finish:
#
#   * magna vereri            -> Web (118), recast until endroll >= WEB_ENDROLL
#                                (vereri don't cast -- a snare/knockdown is the
#                                useful disable).
#   * Ivasian inciter,        -> Corrupt Essence (703): CS vs TD, a failed ward
#     dark-eyed incubus,         drops a "blood red haze" that BLOCKS their
#     pestilent vision           spellcasting ~15s. All three cast, so silencing
#                                them is worth more than a web. 3 mana, once per
#                                target ($ult_silenced_id).
#   * anything unrecognised    -> Web (118), same as -base.
#
# CROWD CONTROL (2026-10-05): the disable above isn't just for the active target.
# Each pass -- and during the DoT hold -- every OTHER hostile in the room gets
# its own disable (703 on casters, 118 on the rest), including anything that
# wanders in mid-fight; with 3+ hostiles (and 2+ groundable ones still
# standing) Grasp of the Grave (709) keeps them on the floor. Mana-gated with a
# reserve for the 710/706 finish. See "crowd control" below; toggle with
# `;vars set ult_cc=off`.
#
# ONE-SHOT ANIMATE BUDDY: the first creature matching animate_target? of a
# hunt (a magna vereri since 2026-10-03; was an incubus for one hunt, and the
# Ivasian inciter before that), if we don't already have an animate up, is handed to `;reanim` (Pain 711 to death, then
# Animate Dead 730 the corpse into a buddy that tanks/attacks for us). Just
# once per hunt -- $ult_reanim_done latches it, and reanim.lic clears that
# latch from its `;reanim die` end-of-hunt teardown (Fizzleworth-prep clears
# it too as a backstop). Every target after the first just gets the normal
# 703 -> 710 -> 706 treatment. This is the mana-conservative middle ground
# between -base (no buddy) and -cat (re-reanims whenever the buddy dies).
#
# The animate is dismissed in the field at end of hunt by
# Fizzleworth-anim-cleanup.lic (weapon back to verlok -> "tell anim die" ->
# ;eloot), same as the -cat variant.
#
# NO VOLN SYMBOLS. Symbol of Retribution and Symbol of Disruption were both
# tried here (2026-09-08 through 09-10) and ripped back out: gs4-wings-compare
# measured Retribution at ~7% of damage for ~300-600 favor/recast, and a
# follow-up run with Disruption alone showed no measurable benefit either --
# neither earned back what it spent, and with everything on Fizzleworth was
# net -450 Voln favor/hunt (favor only refills by releasing undead, so that's
# a real bleed, not noise). If you want to revisit either, the aura-casting
# machinery (cast_voln_aura et al.) is in git history as of this commit.
#
# --- offense finish (identical to -base) --------------------------------
#
#   710 Energy Maelstrom (prep + cast, a DoT) -> 706 Tenebrous Tether (root,
#   only on a pass where 710 actually confirmed cast) -> hold up to
#   MAELSTROM_WAIT for the DoT, bailing on death or the room filling past
#   FLEE_HINT.
#
# Everything casts from stance DEFENSIVE and never leaves it -- per
# https://gswiki.play.net/SMR stance is not a factor for spell SMRv2, and the
# 703/710/706 wards don't care either (kept identical to -base/-cat for
# the comparison). OVEREXERTION: every cast gated on live checkmana vs the
# spell's real cost (Web 118 targeted = 5, Corrupt 703 = 3, Maelstrom 710 =
# 10, Tether 706 = 6). Wound-block ("can't think clearly enough") ->
# ;eherbs --spellcast once. MANA: this rotation keeps the attack script busy
# enough that sac4mana's harvest never gets a window (same as -cat), so
# recovery is INLINE -- at the top of any pass below SACRIFICE_AT: `sacrifice
# mana` (~89, 1 shadow essence) then Symbol of Mana. No pray-for-mana.

# --- knobs -----------------------------------------------------------------

SPELL_WEB_MANA       = 5 unless defined?(SPELL_WEB_MANA)   # TARGETED 118 (not effect-list.xml's 10)
SPELL_CORRUPT_MANA   = (Spell[703].mana_cost.to_i.positive? ? Spell[703].mana_cost.to_i : 3)  unless defined?(SPELL_CORRUPT_MANA)
SPELL_MAELSTROM_MANA = (Spell[710].mana_cost.to_i.positive? ? Spell[710].mana_cost.to_i : 10) unless defined?(SPELL_MAELSTROM_MANA)
SPELL_TETHER_MANA    = (Spell[706].mana_cost.to_i.positive? ? Spell[706].mana_cost.to_i : 6)  unless defined?(SPELL_TETHER_MANA)

WEB_ENDROLL   = 101 unless defined?(WEB_ENDROLL)
WEB_MAX_TRIES = 3   unless defined?(WEB_MAX_TRIES)

MAELSTROM_WAIT = 10 unless defined?(MAELSTROM_WAIT)
FLEE_HINT      = 7  unless defined?(FLEE_HINT)

# While shadow essence is under this, sacrifice the tethered dying target for
# essence during the Maelstrom hold instead of letting the DoT finish it --
# free essence (the kill still counts), and `sacrifice mana` later turns each
# point into ~90 mana. Only fires when the target already appraises
# "enticingly frail", so it never overshoots or wastes a cast.
ESSENCE_LOW      = 4 unless defined?(ESSENCE_LOW)
# Once per hunt, if the buddy's up and mana >= ESSENCE_RUN_MANA but essence <
# ESSENCE_RUN_BELOW, kick off a `;fizzsac` grind to refill the pool. Set
# ESSENCE_RUN_BELOW = 0 to disable the auto-grind (still run ;fizzsac by hand).
ESSENCE_RUN_BELOW = 3   unless defined?(ESSENCE_RUN_BELOW)
ESSENCE_RUN_MANA  = 110 unless defined?(ESSENCE_RUN_MANA)
FRAIL_RE = /enticingly frail|ready to be severed|hovering (?:on|at) the brink|near death/i unless defined?(FRAIL_RE)
SAC_DONE = /forming shadow essence|thrown back in a small blast|unable to complete the link|Roundtime: \d+/i unless defined?(SAC_DONE)

# Top mana off (inline `sacrifice mana`, ~89 for 1 shadow essence) at the start
# of any pass it's below this. Like -cat, ultima keeps the attack script busy
# enough that sac4mana's own harvest never gets a window -- observed OOM at
# 3m33s with 1 Symbol of Mana and 0 sacrifices (2026-09-08). The `;reanim`
# buddy makes it hungrier still, so recovery is inline here.
SACRIFICE_AT = 45 unless defined?(SACRIFICE_AT)

# When a pass can't afford its finish (mana < Maelstrom cost and no recovery
# available -- essence 0 / sacrifice on cooldown), DON'T hand straight back to
# bigshot: it relaunches us immediately, and with `oom: 0` in the profile it
# never rests, so we spun ~380 launches in 3 minutes (3/sec) doing nothing
# while the character stood idle (2026-10-02). Sleep this long first so mana
# regens / sac4mana gets a window, and log it once per OOM_NOTE_EVERY secs.
OOM_BACKOFF    = 4  unless defined?(OOM_BACKOFF)
OOM_NOTE_EVERY = 30 unless defined?(OOM_NOTE_EVERY)

# Creature buckets. vereri -> web; the three casters (inciter/incubus/vision) -> 703.
VERERI_RE  = /magna vereri/i    unless defined?(VERERI_RE)
INCITER_RE = /Ivasian inciter/i unless defined?(INCITER_RE)
INCUBUS_RE = /incubus/i         unless defined?(INCUBUS_RE)
VISION_RE  = /pestilent vision/i unless defined?(VISION_RE)

REANIM_SCRIPT = "reanim" unless defined?(REANIM_SCRIPT)
ANIMATE_SPELL = 730      unless defined?(ANIMATE_SPELL)

# --- patterns ------------------------------------------------------------

CANT_CAST_WOUNDED = /can't think clearly enough to prepare a spell/i unless defined?(CANT_CAST_WOUNDED)

# --- helpers -----------------------------------------------------------

def target_dead?(foe)
  return true if foe.nil?
  return true if foe.status.to_s =~ /dead|gone/
  !GameObj.targets.any? { |t| t.id.to_i == foe.id.to_i && t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ }
end

def living_targets
  GameObj.targets.count { |t| t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ }
end

def essence
  Resources.shadow_essence.to_i
rescue StandardError
  ESSENCE_LOW
end

# Sacrifice the target if the pool's low and it's already frail (tethered from
# land_tether). @return true once it's done for this pass.
def try_essence_harvest(foe)
  return false if target_dead?(foe)
  return false if essence >= ESSENCE_LOW
  s = (Lich::Util.issue_command("appraise ##{foe.id}", /^The .+? is \w+ in size/,
        include_end: false, quiet: true, silent: true) rescue []).join(" ")
  return false unless s =~ FRAIL_RE
  waitrt?
  waitcastrt?
  dothistimeout("sacrifice ##{foe.id}", 5, SAC_DONE)
  waitrt?
  true
end

def hold_for_dot(seconds, foe)
  deadline   = Time.now.to_f + seconds
  harvested  = false
  until Time.now.to_f >= deadline
    return if target_dead?(foe)
    return if living_targets >= FLEE_HINT
    # once, in the back half of the hold: grab it for essence before the DoT
    # kills it (if the pool's low and it's frail)
    if !harvested && Time.now.to_f > deadline - seconds * 0.5
      harvested = try_essence_harvest(foe)
    end
    # idle time between DoT ticks: cover anything that just walked in
    crowd_control(foe) unless target_dead?(foe)
    sleep 0.25
  end
end

# Sends `cmd` and collects every line through the roundtime/resolution message.
# Throw away anything still sitting in our line buffer (a previous cast's tail),
# so the next command's wait-patterns can't match STALE lines.
def drain_lines
  nil while get?
end

# Sends `cmd` and collects every line through the cast's own terminal line
# (its "Cast Roundtime" / refusal). Reads ALL the way to that line -- it used to
# stop early on "blood red haze" / "Warding failed" / "is rooted in place",
# which left the "Cast Roundtime" line unread, and the NEXT cast_collect then
# took that stale line as its own finish and returned instantly (10.05: crowd
# control's 703 -> the main 703 returned early -> `prep 710` matched the 703's
# "Your spell is ready" -> `cast` said "You don't have a spell prepared!").
CAST_DONE = /Cast Roundtime \d+ Sec|Roundtime: \d+ sec|can't think clearly enough to prepare|don't have a spell prepared|^Wait \d+ sec|You can't cast|You have no/i unless defined?(CAST_DONE)

def cast_collect(cmd, timeout = 6)
  lines = []
  drain_lines
  put cmd
  deadline = Time.now.to_f + timeout
  loop do
    line = get?
    if line.nil?
      sleep 0.1
    else
      lines << line
      break if line =~ CAST_DONE
    end
    break if Time.now.to_f >= deadline
  end
  lines.join("\n")
end

def go_defensive
  fput "stance defensive" if stance != "defensive"
end

def vereri?(foe)
  foe && foe.name.to_s =~ VERERI_RE
end

# Which creature becomes the one-shot animate buddy. Measured 2026-10-02..04
# (swings with the claidhmore that landed):
#   Ivasian inciter  ~50-59% (20/34, 7/14) + its own kicks / thorns / chants
#   athletic incubus ~0-9%   (3 of 32)  -- sings, but the weapon never connects
#   magna vereri     ~0-2%   (0-1 of 44) -- ONLY ever swings, and misses
# The vereri is "strongest" but it's useless offensively, so: inciter.
#
# This is a METHOD, not a `FOO = ... unless defined?(FOO)` constant on purpose:
# Lich keeps constants alive across script runs, so a guarded constant keeps
# its OLD value until the whole Lich session restarts (10.03: the vereri
# switch didn't apply to the next hunt for exactly that reason).
def animate_target?(foe)
  foe && foe.name.to_s =~ /Ivasian inciter/i
end

# inciter / incubus / vision -- the three that cast and so get 703
def caster?(foe)
  foe && (foe.name.to_s =~ INCITER_RE || foe.name.to_s =~ INCUBUS_RE || foe.name.to_s =~ VISION_RE)
end

def have_animate?
  return true if $reanim_animate_live          # reanim.lic's source of truth
  GameObj.npcs.any? { |n| n && n.name.to_s =~ /\banimate/i }
rescue StandardError
  false
end

# --- disables --------------------------------------------------------

# Web until the endroll clears WEB_ENDROLL (or WEB_MAX_TRIES). Once per target.
def land_web(foe)
  return if $ult_webbed_id == foe.id.to_i
  tries = 0
  while tries < WEB_MAX_TRIES
    return if target_dead?(foe)
    return if checkmana < SPELL_WEB_MANA
    waitcastrt?
    waitrt?
    text = cast_collect("incant 118")
    if text =~ CANT_CAST_WOUNDED
      Script.run("eherbs", "--spellcast")
      return
    end
    tries += 1
    roll = (text =~ /==\s*\+?(-?\d+)/ ? Regexp.last_match(1).to_i : nil)
    break if (roll && roll >= WEB_ENDROLL) || text =~ /becomes ensnared|is rooted in place/i
    sleep 0.2
  end
  $ult_webbed_id = foe.id.to_i
end

# Corrupt Essence (703) -- silence a caster, once per target.
def land_corrupt(foe)
  return if $ult_silenced_id == foe.id.to_i
  return if target_dead?(foe)
  return if checkmana < SPELL_CORRUPT_MANA
  waitcastrt?
  waitrt?
  text = cast_collect("incant 703")
  if text =~ CANT_CAST_WOUNDED
    Script.run("eherbs", "--spellcast")
    return
  end
  $ult_silenced_id = foe.id.to_i
  waitcastrt?
  waitrt?
end

# prep 710 + cast at foe. @return true only if prep confirmed AND cast went out.
def land_maelstrom(foe)
  return false if target_dead?(foe)
  return false if checkmana < SPELL_MAELSTROM_MANA
  fput "release" if checkprep != "None"
  waitcastrt?
  waitrt?
  drain_lines
  text = dothistimeout("prep 710", 6, /Your spell is ready|can't think clearly enough to prepare/i).to_s
  if text =~ CANT_CAST_WOUNDED
    Script.run("eherbs", "--spellcast")
    return false
  end
  return false unless text =~ /Your spell is ready/i
  return false if target_dead?(foe)
  return false if checkmana < SPELL_MAELSTROM_MANA
  text = cast_collect("cast ##{foe.id}")
  waitcastrt?
  waitrt?
  # `cast` with nothing prepared ("You don't have a spell prepared!") or a
  # refused cast is NOT a landed Maelstrom -- don't go on to tether as if it was.
  return false if text =~ /don't have a spell prepared|^Wait \d+ sec|can't think clearly/i
  true
end

# Tenebrous Tether (706), once per target.
def land_tether(foe)
  return if $ult_tethered_id == foe.id.to_i
  return if target_dead?(foe)
  return if checkmana < SPELL_TETHER_MANA
  waitcastrt?
  waitrt?
  cast_collect("incant 706")
  $ult_tethered_id = foe.id.to_i
  waitcastrt?
  waitrt?
end

# Sacrifice (Mana) has its own cooldown, independent of the other sacrifice
# abilities -- match sac4mana's loose name check rather than an exact key.
def sacrifice_on_cooldown?
  Effects::Cooldowns.to_h.keys.any? { |k| k.to_s =~ /sacrifice\s*\(\s*mana\s*\)/i }
rescue StandardError
  false
end

def shadow_essence
  Resources.shadow_essence.to_i
rescue StandardError
  0
end

# Inline mana top-off: `sacrifice mana` (~89, spends 1 shadow essence) if off
# cooldown with essence to spare, then Symbol of Mana (off-cooldown, deeds to
# spare). sac4mana can't get a harvest window in this rotation, so this is the
# recovery that actually happens mid-hunt.
def recover_mana
  if shadow_essence.positive? && !sacrifice_on_cooldown?
    waitcastrt?
    waitrt?
    r = dothistimeout("sacrifice mana", 4,
          /mana surge into you|overwhelm you with shadow essence|don't have (?:enough|any)/i)
    waitrt?
    return true if r.to_s =~ /mana surge into you|overwhelm you with shadow essence/i
  end
  if !Effects::Cooldowns.active?("Symbol of Mana") && Experience.deeds > 3
    fput "symbol of mana"
    waitrt?
    return true
  end
  false
end

# --- crowd control (2026-10-05) --------------------------------------------
#
# Survivability: don't just disable the ACTIVE target -- disable every hostile
# in the room (703 on the casters, 118 on the rest), including ones that wander
# in mid-fight, and with a crowd drop Grasp of the Grave (709) to keep the
# groundable ones on the floor. Runs at the top of each pass and inside the
# DoT hold (that's idle time anyway). Everything is mana-gated with a reserve
# so the 710/706 finish stays affordable -- this burns mana, so it throttles
# itself when you're low. Knobs are UserVars, read live:
#   ;vars set ult_cc=off              turn crowd control off (default on)
#   ;vars set ult_grasp_at=3          hostiles needed before 709 (default 3)
#   ;vars set ult_cc_reserve=16       mana kept back for the finish (default 16)
#
# Per-creature bookkeeping: $ult_cc[id] = { silenced_at:, webbed: }.

def cc_on?
  v = UserVars.ult_cc
  return true if v.nil?
  return v if v == true || v == false
  v.to_s !~ /\A\s*(?:0|false|off|no)\s*\z/i
end

def cc_int(name, default)
  v = UserVars.send(name)
  v.to_s =~ /\A\s*\d+\s*\z/ ? v.to_i : default
end

CC_SILENCE_GAP = 18 unless defined?(CC_SILENCE_GAP)   # secs before re-silencing the same caster (haze lasts ~15s)
GRASP_GAP      = 6 unless defined?(GRASP_GAP)    # min secs between Grasp casts

def hostiles
  GameObj.targets.select { |t| t && t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ && t.name.to_s !~ /animated|verlok/i }
end

def floored?(t)
  t.status.to_s =~ /lying|prone|sitting|kneeling/i
end

# Can Grasp drag it down? 10.05 log: inciters, incubi AND magna vereri get
# dragged down (one vereri "avoids their clutches"); pestilent visions (noncorporeal
# fliers) never appear in the 709 messages.
def groundable?(t)
  t.name.to_s !~ /pestilent vision/i
end

# Only raise the animate from a LONE target: ;reanim blocks this script ~20s, and
# anything else in the room gets free actions meanwhile (10.05: a second
# inciter's knockdown/stun during exactly that window). `;vars set
# ult_reanim_alone=off` allows reanim with company again.
def reanim_alone_only?
  v = UserVars.ult_reanim_alone
  return true if v.nil?
  return v if v == true || v == false
  v.to_s !~ /\A\s*(?:0|false|off|no)\s*\z/i
end

def others_with(foe)
  hostiles.reject { |t| foe && t.id.to_i == foe.id.to_i }
end

def cc_ok?(cost, reserve = nil)
  checkmana >= cost + (reserve || cc_int(:ult_cc_reserve, 16))
end

# prep + cast `num` at a specific creature id (so the bigshot target isn't touched)
def cast_at(num, id)
  fput "release" if checkprep != "None"
  waitcastrt?
  waitrt?
  drain_lines
  t = dothistimeout("prep #{num}", 6, /Your spell is ready|can't think clearly enough to prepare/i).to_s
  if t =~ CANT_CAST_WOUNDED
    Script.run("eherbs", "--spellcast")
    return nil
  end
  return nil unless t =~ /Your spell is ready/i
  text = cast_collect("cast ##{id}")
  waitcastrt?
  waitrt?
  text
end

def cast_grasp
  waitcastrt?
  waitrt?
  fput "release" if checkprep != "None"
  text = cast_collect("incant 709")
  if text =~ CANT_CAST_WOUNDED
    Script.run("eherbs", "--spellcast")
    return
  end
  $ult_grasp_at = Time.now.to_f
  waitcastrt?
  waitrt?
end

SPELL_GRASP_MANA = (Spell[709].mana_cost.to_i.positive? ? Spell[709].mana_cost.to_i : 9) unless defined?(SPELL_GRASP_MANA)

# One crowd-control action per call (cheap to call often). `foe` is the target
# the main flow is already handling -- skipped here.
def crowd_control(foe, reserve = nil)
  return false unless cc_on?
  all = hostiles
  return false if all.empty?
  now = Time.now.to_f
  $ult_cc ||= {}
  $ult_cc.delete_if { |id, _| all.none? { |t| t.id.to_i == id } }   # forget the dead / gone

  # 1) a crowd -> Grasp, but only if it can still floor 2+ standing creatures
  if all.size >= cc_int(:ult_grasp_at, 3) && now - $ult_grasp_at.to_f > GRASP_GAP &&
     cc_ok?(SPELL_GRASP_MANA, reserve) &&
     all.count { |t| groundable?(t) && !floored?(t) } >= 2
    cast_grasp
    return true
  end

  # 2) disable whoever else is here and still unhandled: casters first (703),
  #    then anything else (118). Web only once per creature; 703 repeats.
  others = all.reject { |t| foe && t.id.to_i == foe.id.to_i }
  others.sort_by { |t| caster?(t) ? 0 : 1 }.each do |t|
    rec = ($ult_cc[t.id.to_i] ||= {})
    if caster?(t)
      next if rec[:silenced_at] && now - rec[:silenced_at] < CC_SILENCE_GAP
      next unless cc_ok?(SPELL_CORRUPT_MANA, reserve)
      cast_at(703, t.id)
      rec[:silenced_at] = now
      return true
    else
      next if rec[:webbed]
      next unless cc_ok?(SPELL_WEB_MANA, reserve)
      cast_at(118, t.id)
      rec[:webbed] = true
      return true
    end
  end
  false
end

# --- main ----------------------------------------------------------

$ult_target      = nil   unless defined?($ult_target)
$ult_webbed_id   = nil   unless defined?($ult_webbed_id)
$ult_silenced_id = nil   unless defined?($ult_silenced_id)
$ult_tethered_id = nil   unless defined?($ult_tethered_id)
$ult_reanim_done = false unless defined?($ult_reanim_done)
$ult_essence_run = false unless defined?($ult_essence_run)   # one fizzsac grind per hunt
$ult_cc          = {}    unless defined?($ult_cc)               # crowd-control bookkeeping per creature id
$ult_grasp_at    = 0.0   unless defined?($ult_grasp_at)
$ult_alone_note  = 0.0   unless defined?($ult_alone_note)

foe = GameObj.targets.find { |t| t.id.to_i == XMLData.current_target_id.to_i } if XMLData.current_target_id
foe ||= GameObj.targets.find { |t| t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ && t.name !~ /animated/ }

exit if target_dead?(foe)

if $ult_target != foe.id.to_i
  $ult_target      = foe.id.to_i
  $ult_webbed_id   = nil
  $ult_silenced_id = nil
  $ult_tethered_id = nil
end

fput "target ##{foe.id}" unless XMLData.current_target_id.to_i == foe.id.to_i
waitrt?
waitcastrt?
exit if target_dead?(foe)

go_defensive

# top mana off before committing to a pass (703 + 710 + 706 + the reanim
# path add up fast, and sac4mana never gets a window here)
recover_mana if checkmana < SACRIFICE_AT

def oom_backoff
  if Time.now.to_f - ($ult_oom_note || 0) > OOM_NOTE_EVERY
    echo "[ultima] out of mana (#{checkmana}) -- backing off #{OOM_BACKOFF}s per pass instead of spinning."
    $ult_oom_note = Time.now.to_f
  end
  sleep OOM_BACKOFF
end

# still too dry for even the cheapest disable (703 = 3) -- back off, then hand back to bigshot
if checkmana < SPELL_CORRUPT_MANA
  oom_backoff
  exit
end

# First animate_target? creature of the hunt with no buddy up -> reanim it
# into one and we're done for this pass (reanim kills it and raises the animate).
if animate_target?(foe) && !$ult_reanim_done && !have_animate? &&
   reanim_alone_only? && !others_with(foe).empty?
  # Not alone: don't reanim now (it'd leave the room unattended for ~20s). Fight
  # it normally; $ult_reanim_done stays false, so the next LONE inciter gets it.
  if Time.now.to_f - $ult_alone_note.to_f > 30
    echo "[ultima] inciter has company (#{others_with(foe).size} other hostile(s)) -- not reanimating; waiting for a lone one."
    $ult_alone_note = Time.now.to_f
  end
elsif animate_target?(foe) && !$ult_reanim_done && !have_animate?
  # ;reanim blocks this script for ~20s (Pain x3, Animate Dead, arming), and no
  # crowd control happens meanwhile -- 10.05 18:04: a second inciter's spell
  # knocked us down (stun 6 rounds, 20s roundtime) during exactly that window.
  # So cover the room FIRST, keeping ~70 mana back so the animate itself stays
  # affordable.
  5.times { break unless crowd_control(foe, 70) }
  Script.run(REANIM_SCRIPT, "##{foe.id}")
  $ult_reanim_done = true
  exit
end

# Once per hunt: buddy is up and mana's healthy but the essence pool is low
# -> grind it back to 5 with `;fizzsac` (pauses bigshot, stops the animate,
# walks creatures to frail + sacrifices, wanders rooms, then hands back).
# `sacrifice mana` needs that pool, so it's worth the interruption.
if !$ult_essence_run && have_animate? &&
   (Resources.shadow_essence.to_i rescue 5) < ESSENCE_RUN_BELOW &&
   checkmana >= ESSENCE_RUN_MANA
  $ult_essence_run = true
  Script.run("fizzsac")
  exit
end

# Crowd control first: disable everyone else in the room, Grasp a crowd.
crowd_control(foe)
exit if target_dead?(foe)

# Creature-specific disable.
if vereri?(foe)
  land_web(foe)
elsif caster?(foe)
  land_corrupt(foe)
else
  land_web(foe)                      # unknown -> web, same as -base
end

# Shared DoT finish.
got_dot = false
unless target_dead?(foe)
  got_dot = land_maelstrom(foe)
  land_tether(foe) if got_dot && !target_dead?(foe)
end

hold_for_dot(MAELSTROM_WAIT, foe) if got_dot

# Nothing landed because we couldn't afford the finish -> don't spin.
oom_backoff if !got_dot && !target_dead?(foe) && checkmana < SPELL_MAELSTROM_MANA

recover_mana if !target_dead?(foe) && checkmana < SACRIFICE_AT
